","27848671"],"issn_org":["27848671"],"issue":"3","journal":"Italian Journal of Dermatology and Venereology","pages":"223-250","publisher":"Edizioni Minerva Medica S.p.A.","status":"p","title":"Italian Journal of Dermatology and Venereology","volume":"159"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194731698"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-beb5cf65-d6b6-4d20-a14c-54f898369933","sdu-3b8af482-5af2-4494-8f45-cc5ce8efbe67"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Italian S3-Guideline on the treatment of Atopic Eczema - Part 1 : Systemic therapy, adapted from EuroGuiDerm by the Italian Society of Dermatology and STD (SIDEMAST), the Italian Association of Hospital Dermatologists (ADOI) and the Italian Society of Allergological and Environmental Dermatology (SIDAPA)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-742030","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Now extinct, the aurochs (Bos primigenius) was a keystone species in prehistoric Eurasian and North African ecosystems, and the progenitor of cattle (Bos taurus), domesticates that have provided people with food and labour for millennia1. Here we analysed 38 ancient genomes and found 4 distinct population ancestries in the aurochs—European, Southwest Asian, North Asian and South Asian—each of which has dynamic trajectories that have responded to changes in climate and human influence. Similarly to Homo heidelbergensis, aurochsen first entered Europe around 650 thousand years ago2, but early populations left only trace ancestry, with both North Asian and European B. primigenius genomes coalescing during the most recent glaciation. North Asian and European populations then appear separated until mixing after the climate amelioration of the early Holocene. European aurochsen endured the more severe bottleneck during the Last Glacial Maximum, retreating to southern refugia before recolonizing from Iberia. Domestication involved the capture of a small number of individuals from the Southwest Asian aurochs population, followed by early and pervasive male-mediated admixture involving each ancestral strain of aurochs after domestic stocks dispersed beyond their cradle of origin.","author_count":51,"contributors":["Rossi, Conor","Sinding, Mikkel Holger S.","Mullin, Victoria E.","Scheu, Amelie","Erven, Jolijn A.M.","Verdugo, Marta Pereira","Daly, Kevin G.","Ciucani, Marta Maria","Mattiangeli, Valeria","Teasdale, Matthew D.","Diquelou, Deborah","Manin, Aurélie","Bangsgaard, Pernille","Collins, Matthew J.","Lord, Tom C.","Zeibert, Viktor","Zorzin, Roberto","Vinter, Michael","Timmons, Zena","Kitchener, Andrew C.","Street, Martin","Haruda, Ashleigh F.","Tabbada, Kristina","Larson, Greger","Frantz, Laurent A.F.","Gehlen, Birgit","Alhaique, Francesca","Tagliacozzo, Antonio","Fornasiero, Mariagabriella","Pandolfi, Luca","Karastoyanova, Nadezhda","Sørensen, Lasse","Kiryushin, Kirill","Ekström, Jonas","Mostadius, Maria","Grandal-d’Anglade, Aurora","Vidal-Gorosquieta, Amalia","Benecke, Norbert","Kropp, Claus","Grushin, Sergei P.","Gilbert, M. Thomas P.","Merts, Ilja","Merts, Viktor","Outram, Alan K.","Rosengren, Erika","Kosintsev, Pavel","Sablin, Mikhail","Tishkin, Alexey A.","Makarewicz, Cheryl A.","Burger, Joachim","Bradley, Daniel G."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776896"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Central","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Bulgaria","Germany","Ireland","Israel","Italy","Kazakhstan","Netherlands","Russia","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Al Farabi Kazakh National University","All Global Affiliations","Altai State University","Archaeological Research Centre and Museum for Human Behavioural Evolution","Bulgarian Academy of Sciences","Centre for Palaeogenetics","German Archaeological Institute","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","Kiel University","Lauresham Laboratory for Experimental Archaeology","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Lund University","Museo Civico di Storia Naturale di Verona","Museo della Natura e dell’ Uomo","Museo delle Civiltà","National Museums of Scotland","Queen Mary University of London","RAS - Institute of Plant and Animal Ecology, Ural Branch","Russian Academy of Sciences","S. Toraighyrov Pavlodar State University","Trinity College Dublin","University College Dublin","University of A Coruna","University of Cambridge","University of Cologne","University of Edinburgh","University of Exeter","University of Groningen","University of Haifa","University of Newcastle","University of Oxford","University of Pisa","Ural Federal University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"],"OT":["Vendsyssel Historiske Museum"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the genomic natural history of the aurochs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-776896","identifier":[{"id":"39478219","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85208020499","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-09402bb8-fcbf-4b23-96ba-b196f4fa3003"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D1C333FDB4E16ED23F769C5C232606E0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ie","key":"trinity college dublin","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Trinity College Dublin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Computational and RNA Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"johannes gutenberg university mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"university of groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Groningen","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ie","key":"university college dublin","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University College Dublin","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"university of newcastle","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Newcastle","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"kz","key":"al farabi