{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Neumayer, Christina","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383742"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"seeing images from conflict through computer vision","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.taylorfrancis.com/chapters/edit/10.4324/9781003176923-9/seeing-images-conflict-computer-vision-christina-neumayer-luca-rossi","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383742","ids":["itu-aa9b98a9-d60d-41b3-a3d6-a993f23aec50"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DEC2B03E6CC6F563C20BD45C94D8803F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.taylorfrancis.com/chapters/edit/10.4324/9781003176923-9/seeing-images-conflict-computer-vision-christina-neumayer-luca-rossi","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human Data Interaction Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human-Centered Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"neumayerpau","last":"Neumayer","name":"Neumayer, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781003176923"],"pages":"122","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Social Media Images and Conflicts"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-aa9b98a9-d60d-41b3-a3d6-a993f23aec50"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Seeing Images from Conflict through Computer Vision","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383742","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Social media represent an important source of news for many users. They are, however, affected by misinformation and they might be playing a role in the growth of political polarization. In this paper, we create an agent based model to investigate how policing content and backlash on social media (i.e. conflict) can lead to an increase in polarization for both users and news sources. Our model is an advancement over previously proposed models because it allows us to study the polarization of both users and news sources, the evolution of the audience connections between users and sources, and it makes more realistic assumptions about the starting conditions of the system. We find that the tendency of users and sources to avoid policing, backlash and conflict in general can increase polarization online. Specifically polarization comes from the ease of sharing political posts, intolerance for opposing points of view causing backlash and policing, and volatility in changing one’s opinion when faced with new information. On the other hand, it seems that the integrity of a news source in trying to resist the backlash and policing has little effect.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Coscia, Michele","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384617"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agent based model","Misinformation","Online conflict","Political polarization","Social media"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how minimizing conflicts could lead to polarization on social media an agent based model investigation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0263184","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384617","identifier":[{"id":"85123604649","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e350f1b1-e3c2-461e-94c6-acfa6115af8e"],"keyword":["Agent-based model","Misinformation","Online conflict","Political polarization","Social media"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4D4C503CBD8568CFAEC5C93500D33728"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0263184","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0263184","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"cosciapau","last":"Coscia","locid":"90b501a9-4d44-460b-b193-4d7d524bb21b","name":"Coscia, Michele","orcid":"0000-0001-5984-5137","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0263184","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"1","journal":"PLOS ONE","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123604649"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e350f1b1-e3c2-461e-94c6-acfa6115af8e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How minimizing conflicts could lead to polarization on social media: An agent-based model investigation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384617","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Rationale: Lung biopsy (LBx) has a relevant role in the prediction of prognosis of interstitial lung diseases (ILDs), but its impact on the clinical management of patients remains unexplored. Objectives: This study evaluates whether LBx may change the therapeutic strategy and assesses the effect of diagnostic reclassification after LBx on long-term prognosis. Methods: We evaluated the LBx of 426 consecutive patients with ILDs, without a definite usual interstitial pneumonia pattern on high-resolution computed tomographic imaging. A total of 266 patients underwent transbronchial lung cryobiopsy (TBLC), and 160 patients underwent surgical lung biopsy (SLB). The multidisciplinary team (MDT) determined a diagnosis with high or low confidence, and a management strategy, both before and after the LBx data. Results: Final MDT diagnoses were 189 idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis (IPF), 143 non-IPF fibrotic ILDs, and 94 nonfibrotic ILDs. LBx data changed the management strategy in 145 cases (34%), with similar results for TBLC and SLB (the treatment strategy changed in 31.5% of TBLC cases, 84/266, P < 0.001, and in 38% of SLB, 61/160, P < 0.001). After LBx, the MDT was less inclined to \"wait and see\" (from 15% to 4% of cases, P < 0.001) or to prescribe steroids only (from 54% to 37%, P < 0.001) and was more confident to treat with antifibrotics (from 23% to 44%, P < 0.001) or immunosuppressive drugs (from 7% to 14%, P < 0.001). The therapeutic strategy changed in 70% of reclassified cases (60/85) and in 59% of cases in which LBx increased the MDT confidence (84/142). Reclassification significantly impacted the outcome. The cases classified as non-IPF by clinician and radiologist and then reclassified to be IPF after LBx showed a significantly worse survival compared with non-IPF confirmed cases (adjusted hazard ratio [HR], 3.8; 95% confidence interval [CI], 1.75-8.3); P = 0.001. Cases initially classified as IPF and then reclassified as non-IPF after LBx showed a better prognosis compared with IPF confirmed cases (HR, 0.41; 95% CI, 0.18-0.94; P = 0.03). Conclusions: Reclassification of cases with LBx data increased diagnostic confidence and changed the therapeutic strategy in one-third of cases. Pathologic reclassification of cases refined prognosis prediction. Patients classified as non-IPF by clinician and radiologist and then reclassified IPF after LBx had worse prognosis compared with the non-IPF confirmed cases.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Tomassetti, Sara","Ravaglia, Claudia","Puglisi, Silvia","Ryu, Jay H.","Colby, Thomas V.","Cavazza, Alberto","Wells, Athol U.","Pavone, Mauro","Vancheri, Carlo","Lavorini, Federico","Matucci-Cerinic, Marco","Rosi, Elisabetta","Luzzi, Valentina","Gori, Leonardo","Rossi, Giulio","Donati, Luca","Dubini, Alessandra","Piciucchi, Sara","Poletti, Venerino"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-237072"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Azienda Ospedaliera Careggi","Azienda Ospedaliero-Universitaria policlinico - Vittorio Emanuele","Imperial College London","Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN","Mayo Clinic Scottsdale, AZ","Morgagni-Pierantoni Hospital","University of Modena and Reggio Emilia"],"keyword":["Idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis","Interstitial lung diseases","Surgical lung biopsy","Transbronchial lung cryobiopsy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of lung biopsy information on treatment strategy of patients with interstitial lung diseases","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":