{"abstract":"The information on a quantum process acquired through measurements plays a crucial role in the determination of its nonequilibrium thermodynamic properties. We report on the experimental inference of the stochastic entropy production rate for a continuously monitored mesoscopic quantum system. We consider an optomechanical system subjected to continuous displacement Gaussian measurements and characterize the entropy production rate of the individual trajectories followed by the system in its stochastic dynamics, employing a phase-space description in terms of the Wigner entropy. Owing to the specific regime of our experiment, we are able to single out the informational contribution to the entropy production arising from conditioning the state on the measurement outcomes. Our experiment embodies a significant step towards the demonstration of full-scale control of fundamental thermodynamic processes at the mesoscopic quantum scale.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rossi, Massimiliano","Mancino, Luca","Landi, Gabriel T.","Paternostro, Mauro","Schliesser, Albert","Belenchia, Alessio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-479627"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen's University Belfast","Universidade de São Paulo"],"keyword":["Quantum control"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental assessment of entropy production in a continuously measured mechanical resonator","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/247982394/PhysRevLett.125.080601.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-479627","identifier":[{"id":"85090820936","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32909766","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000560626400003","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-903b296b-b121-4826-a520-486503c640b5"],"keyword":["QUANTUM CONTROL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1C4053EBE89C6A48B59DCF32A5306D09"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/247982394/PhysRevLett.125.080601.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Quantop"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"queen s university belfast","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen's University Belfast","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"br","key":"universidade de são paulo","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Universidade de São Paulo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Massimiliano","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"a0e99398-a857-43e5-9d4b-6a82b46ddec3","name":"Rossi, Massimiliano","orcid":"0000-0001-8992-3378","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Luca","key":"mancinopau","last":"Mancino","name":"Mancino, Luca","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Gabriel T.","key":"landipau","last":"Landi","name":"Landi, Gabriel T.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mauro","key":"paternostropau","last":"Paternostro","name":"Paternostro, Mauro","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"mwh574","key":"mwh574pau","last":"mwh574","locid":"8e997286-0f6b-4ef3-b311-d10021f02074","name":"Schliesser, Albert","name_org":"mwh574, mwh574","orcid":"0000-0003-4317-5030","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Alessio","key":"belenchiapau","last":"Belenchia","name":"Belenchia, Alessio","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32909766"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevlett.125.080601","issn":["00319007","10797114"],"issn_org":["00319007"],"issue":"8","journal":"Physical Review Letters","paperid":"080601","status":"p","title":"Physical Review Letters","volume":"125"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090820936"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-903b296b-b121-4826-a520-486503c640b5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Experimental Assessment of Entropy Production in a Continuously Measured Mechanical Resonator","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-479627","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Over the last few years, a proliferation of attempts to define, understand and fight the spread of problematic information in contemporary media ecosystems emerged. Most of these attempts focus on false content and/or bad actors detection. In this paper, we argue for a wider ecological focus. Using the frame of media manipulation and a revised version of the ‘coordinated inauthentic behavior’ original definition, the paper presents a study based on an unprecedented combination of Facebook data, accessed through the CrowdTangle API, and two datasets of Italian political news stories published in the run-up to the 2018 Italian general election and 2019 European election. By focusing on actors’ collective behavior, we identified several networks of pages, groups, and verified public profiles (‘entities’), that shared the same political news articles on Facebook within a very short period of time. Some entities in our networks were openly political, while others, despite sharing political content too, deceptively presented themselves as entertainment venues. The proportion of inauthentic entities in a network affects the wideness of the range of news media sources they shared, thus pointing to different strategies and possible motivations. The paper has both theoretical and empirical implications: it frames the concept of ‘coordinated inauthentic behavior’ in existing literature, introduces a method to detect coordinated link sharing behavior and points out different strategies and methods employed by networks of actors willing to manipulate the media and public opinion.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Giglietto, Fabio","Righetti, Nicola","Rossi, Luca","Marino, Giada"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382414"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universita' degli Studi de Urbino Carlo Bo"],"keyword":["Authenticity","CrowdTangle","Elections","Facebook","Italy","Political news","coordinated inauthentic behavior"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"it takes a village to manipulate the media coordinated link sharing behavior during 000000002018 and 000000002019 italian elections","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85402374/It_takes_a_village_to_manipulate_the_media.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382414","identifier":[{"id":"85081723807","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4c6d8740-a425-4378-b6df-b4543874972d"],"keyword":["CrowdTangle","Facebook","Italy","authenticity","coordinated inauthentic behavior","elections","political news"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-99C1BD0ED6E8056A9F846C2262577F99"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85402374/It_takes_a_village_to_manipulate_the_media.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"universita degli studi de urbino carlo bo","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universita' degli Studi de Urbino Carlo Bo","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human Data Interaction Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio","key":"gigliettopau","last":"Giglietto","name":"Giglietto, Fabio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicola","key":"righettipau","last":"Righetti","name":"Righetti, Nicola","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giada","key":"marinopau","last":"Marino","name":"Marino, Giada","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/1369118x.2020.1739732","issn":["1369118X","14684462"],"issn_org":["1369118X"],"issue":"25","journal":"Information, Communication & Society","pages":"867","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Information, Communication & Society","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081723807"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4c6d8740-a425-4378-b6df-b4543874972d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"It takes a village to manipulate the media: coordinated link sharing behavior during 2018 and 2019 Italian elections.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382414","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this research we ask which role humorous social media images play for the representation of political protest in social media. To do so, we collected tweets (n=678946) based on protest hashtags from the G20 protests in Hamburg July 6-8 2017. With a social network analysis we find that while we can see clusters around user accounts of activist collectives, media institutions, and authorities (such as the Hamburg police), we cannot observe a network centred around user accounts of residents of Hamburg. As seemingly neutral humorous perspectives which do neither take the side of the activists or the authorities, these images seem to be shared across various clusters in the network. Yet, these are among the most frequently shared tweets based on number of retweets and mentions. Through a narrative analysis of the most frequently shared tweets with a particular focus on such humorous juxtapositions of the protests and the everyday life of residents, we find that these seemingly apolitical images and videos shared across communities, still play a disruptive role in the narrative about political protest. We argue that the privileging of humorous content that users are perhaps more inclined to share in social media than political messages, activists’ grievances or violent imagery, might (while not actively taking sides) push activists’ grievances in the background and make their actions appear as disruptive. With these findings, this research contributes to furthering our understanding of how the logics of social media might influence narratives of contemporary protests.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Neumayer, Christina","Rossi, Luca","Jensen, Minna S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-462605"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"disruptive humour a citizen perspective in social media images from mass protests","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5210/spir.v2020i0.11288","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-462605","ids":["ku-73abb1a9-7e31-4fc5-967e-22a345e8cef9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F612EF5A53226992C98AE96984030144"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5210/spir.v2020i0.11288","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"neumayerpau","last":"Neumayer","locid":"15f1c085-b93f-40cc-9ef6-b8ae24783438","name":"Neumayer, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-0450-2983","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","name":"Rossi, Luca","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Minna S.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Minna S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5210/spir.v2020i0.11288","status":"p","subtitle":"The 21th Annual Conference of the Association of Internet Researchers","title":"AoIR Selected Papers of Internet Research","volume":"2020: AoIR2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-73abb1a9-7e31-4fc5-967e-22a345e8cef9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Disruptive humour: a citizen perspective in social media images from mass protests","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-462605","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Transbronchial lung cryobiopsy (TBLC) has been introduced recently in the diagnosis of interstitial lung diseases. We aimed to evaluate the prognostic significance of the distinction between idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis and other interstitial lung diseases with the use of TBLC data in multidisciplinary team (MDT) diagnosis. Methods: In this single-centre, retrospective, investigator-initiated comparative study, we evaluated consecutive patients without a definite usual interstitial pneumonia pattern on high-resolution CT, who presented to the GB Morgagni Hospital (Forlì, Italy), and who underwent TBLC (Jan 1, 2011, to Dec 31, 2014) or surgical lung biopsy (SLB; Jan 1, 2002, to Dec 31, 2016). Three pathologists reviewed the specimens, masked to clinical information. MDT evaluation was done before and after biopsy. The primary endpoint was the prognostic significance of the MDT diagnostic separation between idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis and other interstitial lung diseases in patients undergoing TBLC. Mortality was evaluated by means of Cox regression analysis. Findings: We evaluated 500 consecutive cases, 426 of which were included: 266 had TBLC and 160 had SLB. 189 patients had idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis, 143 had other fibrotic interstitial lung diseases, and 94 had non-fibrotic interstitial lung diseases. Patients undergoing TBLC had more comorbidities and better preserved lung function compared with those undergoing SLB; among patients with a final MDT diagnosis of idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis, patients undergoing TBLC were older, had more comorbidities, and had a different post-biopsy treatment profile than those who received SLB. The distinction between idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis and other interstitial lung diseases made by MDT diagnosis on the basis of TBLC biopsy had clear prognostic significance, with a 5-year transplant-free survival of 68% (95% CI 57–76) in patients with an MDT idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis diagnosis based on TBLC compared with 93% (87–96) in patients without an idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis diagnosis based on TBLC (hazard ratio 5·28, 95% CI 2·72–10·04; p<0·0001). This distinction remained statistically significant in a multivariate analysis controlling for age, sex, smoking status, comorbidities, pulmonary function, and high-resolution CT patterns (p=0·02). Interpretation: TBLC makes an important diagnostic contribution in interstitial lung disease, on the basis of the prognostic distinction between idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis and other interstitial lung diseases when TBLC findings are included in multidisciplinary diagnosis. Funding: None.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Tomassetti, Sara","Ravaglia, Claudia","Wells, Athol U.","Cavazza, Alberto","Colby, Thomas V.","Rossi, Giulio","Ley, Brett","Ryu, Jay H.","Puglisi, Silvia","Arcadu, Antonella","Marchi, Martina","Sultani, Fabio","Martinello, Sabrina","Donati, Luca","Gurioli, Carlo","Gurioli, Christian","Tantalocco, Paola","Hetzel, Jurgen","Dubini, Alessandra","Piciucchi, Sara","Klersy, Catherine","Lavorini, Federico","Poletti, Venerino"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-266342"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Tomassetti, Sara"],"country":["Germany","Italy","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Azienda Ospedaliera Careggi","IRCCS Azienda Unità Sanitaria Locale di Reggio Emilia","IRCCS Fondazione Policlinico San Matteo - Pavia","Imperial College London","Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN","Mayo Clinic Scottsdale, AZ","Morgagni-Pierantoni Hospital","University of Arizona","University of California at San Francisco","University of Tübingen"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3