alysis of the Consequences of the General Data Protection Regulation on Social Network Research","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382391","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Bipartite networks are a well known strategy to study a variety of phenomena. The commonly used method to deal with this type of network is to project the bipartite data into a unipartite weighted graph and then using a backboning technique to extract only the meaningful edges. Despite the wide availability of different methods both for projection and backboning, we believe that there has been little attention to the effect that the combination of these two processes has on the data and on the resulting network topology. In this paper we study the effect that the possible combinations of projection and backboning techniques have on a bipartite network. We show that the 12 methods group into two clusters producing unipartite networks with very different topologies. We also show that the resulting level of network centralization is highly affected by the combination of projection and backboning applied.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Coscia, Michele","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382397"],"event":{"acronym":"ASONAM","title":"IEEE/ACM International Conference on Advances in Social Networks Analysis and Mining"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Complex networks","network backboning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of projection and backboning on network topologies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3341161.3342862","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382397","identifier":[{"id":"85078831994","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4b76fefe-7068-423c-97bf-4bace068e6c2"],"keyword":["complex networks","network backboning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B1E769A7A6687645072673D024FD4C32"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84366334/The_Impact_of_Projection_and_Backboning_on_Network_Topologies.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3341161.3342862","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"cosciapau","last":"Coscia","locid":"90b501a9-4d44-460b-b193-4d7d524bb21b","name":"Coscia, Michele","orcid":"0000-0001-5984-5137","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3341161.3342862","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"International Conference on Advances in Social Networks Analysis and Mining"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078831994"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4b76fefe-7068-423c-97bf-4bace068e6c2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Impact of Projection and Backboning on Network Topologies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382397","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We propose a way to model topic-based implicit interactions among Twitter users. Our model relies on grouping Twitter hashtags, in a given context, into themes/topics and then using the multiplex network model to construct a thematic multiplex where each layer corresponds to a topic/theme, and users within a layer are connected if and only if they used the same hashtag. We show, by testing our model on a real-world Twitter dataset, that applying multiplex community detection on the thematic multiplex can reveal new types of communities that were not observed before using the traditional ways of modeling Twitter interactions","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hanteer, Obaida","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382441"],"event":{"acronym":"ICWSM","title":"International AAAI Conference on Web and Social Media"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Community detection","Multiplex network","Social media modeling","Thematic analysis","Twitter interactions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an innovative way to model twitter topic driven interactions using multiplex networks","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fdata.2019.00009","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382441","identifier":[{"id":"85076679452","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4ea232c8-59df-4ed9-a5af-93292f5ce16c"],"keyword":["Community detection","Multiplex network","Social media modeling","Thematic analysis","Twitter interactions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-69166476470DBB353312B0BDA01AB219"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84823763/fdata_02_00009.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fdata.2019.00009","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Obaida","key":"hanteerpau","last":"Hanteer","name":"Hanteer, Obaida","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fdata.2019.00009","publisher":"Frontiers","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Big Data. Workshop Proceedings of the 13th International AAAI Conference on Web and Social Media"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076679452"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4ea232c8-59df-4ed9-a5af-93292f5ce16c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An Innovative Way to Model Twitter Topic-Driven Interactions Using Multiplex Networks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382441","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Alarmed by the oversimplifications related to the ‘fake news’ buzzword, researchers have started to unpack the concept, defining diverse types and forms of misleading news. Most of the existing works in the area consider crucial the intent of the content creator in order to differentiate among different types of problematic information. This article argues for a change of perspective that, by leveraging the conceptual framework of sociocybernetics, shifts from exclusive attention to creators of misleading information to a broader approach that focuses on propagators and, as a result, on the dynamics of the propagation processes. The analytical implications of this perspective are discussed at a micro level (criteria to judge the falsehood of news and to decide to spread it), at a meso level (four possible relations between individual judgements and decisions), and at a macro level (global circulation cascades). The authors apply this theoretical gaze to analyse ‘fake news’ stories that challenge existing models.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Giglietto, Fabio","Iannelli, Laura","Valeriani, Augusto","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381254"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universita' degli Studi de Urbino Carlo Bo","University of Bologna","University of Sassari"],"keyword":["Fake news","Hybrid media system","Misinformation","Social media","sociocybernetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fake news is the invention of a liar how false information circulates within the hybrid news system","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83995855/CSI837536_fg_av_lr.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381254","identifier":[{"id":"85064223856","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-00650f54-dadd-49a6-8500-e17e837197cb"],"keyword":["Fake news","hybrid media system","misinformation","social media","sociocybernetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6FD5C05E8C56D17B89489B19FB54F83F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83995855/CSI837536_fg_av_lr.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"universita degli studi de urbino carlo bo","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universita' degli Studi de Urbino Carlo Bo","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of sassari","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sassari","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human Data Interaction Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio","key":"gigliettopau","last":"Giglietto","name":"Giglietto, Fabio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"iannellipau","last":"Iannelli","name":"Iannelli, Laura","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Augusto","key":"valerianipau","last":"Valeriani","name":"Valeriani, Augusto","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0011392119837536","issn":["00113921","14617064"],"issn_org":["00113921"],"journal":"Current Sociology","pages":"1-18","publisher":"Sage Publishing","status":"p","title":"Current Sociology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064223856"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-00650f54-dadd-49a6-8500-e17e837197cb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"‘Fake news’ is the invention of a liar: How false information circulates within the hybrid news system","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381254","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The ongoing radical transformations in communication ecosystems have brought up concerns about the risks of partisan selective exposure and ideological polarization. Traditionally, partisan selective exposure is measured by cross-tabulating survey responses to questions on vote intentions and media consumption. This process is expensive, limits the number of news outlets taken into account and is prone to the typical biases of self-reported data. Building upon previous works and with a specific focus on the online media...","author_count":4,"contributors":["Giglietto, Fabio","Righetti, Nicola","Marino, Giada","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384723"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universita' degli Studi de Urbino Carlo Bo"],"keyword":["Attention","Italian 2018 election","Polarization","Selective exposure","insularity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multi party media partisanship attention score estimating partisan attention of news media sources using twitter data in the lead up to 000000002018 italian election","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84084974/07_Giglietto_etal_rev2.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384723","identifier":[{"id":"85067663157","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ea280c2f-ac40-4049-a745-b1e127f8508e"],"keyword":["Attention","Italian 2018 election","insularity","polarization","selective exposure"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F75DBAB4BACCC99F1B790295440C4B0A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84084974/07_Giglietto_etal_rev2.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"universita degli studi de urbino carlo bo","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universita' degli Studi de Urbino Carlo Bo","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human Data Interaction Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio","key":"gigliettopau","last":"Giglietto","name":"Giglietto, Fabio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicola","key":"righettipau","last":"Righetti","name":"Righetti, Nicola","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giada","key":"marinopau","last":"Marino","name":"Marino, Giada","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3270/93030","issn":["15946061","19725094"],"issn_org":["15946061"],"journal":"Comunicazione Politica","pages":"85-108","publisher":"Societa Editrice Il Mulino","publisher_org":"Societa Editrice IlMulino","status":"p","title":"Comunicazione Politica"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067663157"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ea280c2f-ac40-4049-a745-b1e127f8508e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multi-Party Media Partisanship Attention Score. Estimating Partisan Attention of News Media Sources Using Twitter Data in the Lead-up to 2018 Italian Election","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384723","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This article explores user motivations for sharing and creating internet memes in a crisis situation. For this purpose, we investigate the kitten memes in #Brusselslockdown on Twitter, following the Brussels security lockdown in November 2015 that resulted from information about potential terrorist attacks. We use a social network analysis to identify three user groups: content producers, content sharers, and conversationalists. On the basis of interviews with users from these three groups, we argue that the motivations for sharing and creating memes range from personal involvement in the crisis situation to acts of resistance to creative self-realization. We conclude by arguing that a combination of motifs and activities employ the visuality of internet memes to express popular internet culture, resistance, and solidarity as well as a humorous means of coping with the crisis situation. As a form of solidarity beyond the political, internet memes create tension between a crisis event, the mundane, terror, resistance, and humor.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Minna","Neumayer, Christina","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382766"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Brusselslockdown","Crisis communication","Internet memes","Social network analysis","User motivations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"brussels will land on its feet like a cat motivations for memefying brusselslockdown","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83155344/ICS_MSJ_CN_LR.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382766","identifier":[{"id":"85048827720","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-63c43606-a25c-4c31-83ab-82601fd349f1"],"keyword":["#Brusselslockdown","Crisis communication","Internet memes","Social network analysis","User motivations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FEE3826EDD1B04975ED14997616D0BF1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83155344/ICS_MSJ_CN_LR.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Minna","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Minna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"neumayerpau","last":"Neumayer","name":"Neumayer, Christina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/1369118x.2018.1486866","issn":["1369118X","14684462"],"issn_org":["1369118X"],"journal":"Information, Communication & Society","pages":"1-17","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Information, Communication & Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048827720"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-63c43606-a25c-4c31-83ab-82601fd349f1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"‘Brussels will land on its feet like a cat’: motivations for memefying #Brusselslockdown","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382766","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
