e":"Facebook shuts the gate after the horse has bolted, and hurts real research in the process","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-131057","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In the context of community detection in online social media, a lot of effort has been put into the definition of sophisticated network clustering algorithms and much less on the equally crucial process of obtaining high-quality input data. User-interaction data explicitly provided by social media platforms has largely been used as the main source of data because of its easy accessibility. However, this data does not capture a fundamental and much more frequent type of participatory behavior where users do not explicitly mention others but direct their messages to an invisible audience following a common hashtag. In the context of multiplex community detection, we show how to construct an additional data layer about user participation not relying on explicit interactions between users, and how this layer can be used to find different types of communities in the context of Twitter political communication.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hanteer, Obaida","Rossi, Luca","D'aurelio, Davide Vega","Magnani, Matteo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383338"],"event":{"acronym":"ASONAM","title":"IEEE/ACM International Conference on Advances in Social Networks Analysis and Mining"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Community detection","Multiplex Community Detection","Network Clustering Algorithms","Online Social Media","User Interaction Data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from interaction to participation the role of the imagined audience in social media community detection and an application to political communication on twitter","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83570712/ASONAM2018_paper_109.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383338","identifier":[{"id":"85057334859","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8d118d7c-e686-491f-9b0e-80e9e9d890f5"],"keyword":["Community Detection","Multiplex Community Detection","Network Clustering Algorithms","Online Social Media","User-Interaction Data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2A9D957197F762C314377AABEB31EB8B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83570712/ASONAM2018_paper_109.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Obaida","key":"hanteerpau","last":"Hanteer","name":"Hanteer, Obaida","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Davide Vega","key":"daureliopau","last":"D'aurelio","name":"D'aurelio, Davide Vega","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matteo","key":"magnanipau","last":"Magnani","name":"Magnani, Matteo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/asonam.2018.8508575","eisbn":["9781538660515"],"isbn":["9781538660522"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2018 IEEE/ACM International Conference on Advances in Social Networks Analysis and Mining (ASONAM)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057334859"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8d118d7c-e686-491f-9b0e-80e9e9d890f5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"From Interaction to Participation: The Role of the Imagined Audience in Social Media Community Detection and an Application to Political Communication on Twitter","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383338","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"While political protest is essentially a visual expression of dissent, both social movement research and media studies have thus far been hesitant to focus on visual social media data from protest events. This research explores the visual dimension (photos and videos) of Twitter communication in the Blockupy protests against the opening of the European Central Bank headquarters in Frankfurt am Main on 18 March 2015. It does so through a novel combination of quantitative analysis, content analysis of images, and identification of narratives. The article concludes by arguing that the visual in political protest in social media reproduces existing visualities and hierarchies rather than challenges them. This research enhances our conceptual understanding of how activists’ struggles play out in the visual and contributes to developing methods for empirical inquiry into visual social media content.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Neumayer, Christina","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383971"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blockupy","Images","Protest","Social media","Social movements","Twitter","Visual analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"images of protest in social media struggle over visibility and visual narratives","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83039148/NMS_Neumayer_Rossi_preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383971","identifier":[{"id":"85055731993","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b8bec3e3-220b-4bfe-9a21-9e15058e3f32"],"keyword":["Blockupy","Images","Twitter","protest","social media","social movements","visual analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1653F66A5A8249C0E0021CE6D9CDBFAC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83039148/NMS_Neumayer_Rossi_preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"neumayerpau","last":"Neumayer","name":"Neumayer, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1461444818770602","issn":["14614448","14617315"],"issn_org":["14614448"],"issue":"11","journal":"New Media & Society","pages":"1-18","publisher":"Sage Publishing","status":"p","title":"New Media & Society","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055731993"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b8bec3e3-220b-4bfe-9a21-9e15058e3f32"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Images of protest in social media: Struggle over visibility and visual narratives","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383971","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"How do teens deal with the complexities of the digital world? Although many scholars have asked this question, few have considered not only the interpersonal concerns that loom large in the lives of teens and young adults but also their relationship with the social media platforms which have become so central to their lives. In this paper we present a study of Danish teens’ attitudes towards social media platforms they use most – Facebook and Snapchat. We find gender differences in attitudes toward each platform. We also illustrate the potential role of a digital education effort in changing teen attitudes.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Villebro, Mikkel","Shklovski, Irina","Rossi, Luca","Bhørstorp, Alex"],"cuid":["S02-080.91-031076"],"event":{"acronym":"SM&S","end":"2018-07-20","place":"Frederiksberg, dk","start":"2018-07-18","title":"The 9th International Conference on Social Media &amp; Society. SMSociety 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Attitude change","Danish teens","Digital education","Facebook","Gender differences","Interpersonal concerns","Online interaction","Platforms","Privacy","Snapchat","Social media","Social media platforms","Teen digital behavior","Teens","Trust"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comfortably numb danish teens attitudes towards social media platforms","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83271316/p187_villebro.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-080.91-031076","identifier":[{"id":"85051473071","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-039fe36b-0f71-4fd9-baa9-3a567fe