rstorp, Alex","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anatoliy","key":"gruzdpedh","last":"Gruzd","name":"Gruzd, Anatoliy","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jenna","key":"jacobsonpedh","last":"Jacobson","name":"Jacobson, Jenna","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Philip","key":"maipedh","last":"Mai","name":"Mai, Philip","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jeff","key":"hemsleypedh","last":"Hemsley","name":"Hemsley, Jeff","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"K. Hazel","key":"kwonpedh","last":"Kwon","name":"Kwon, K. Hazel","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ravi","key":"vatrapupedh","last":"Vatrapu","name":"Vatrapu, Ravi","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anabel","key":"quanhaasepedh","last":"Quan-Haase","name":"Quan-Haase, Anabel","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Luke","key":"sloanpedh","last":"Sloan","name":"Sloan, Luke","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jaigris","key":"hodsonpedh","last":"Hodson","name":"Hodson, Jaigris","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3217804.3217911","eisbn":["9781450363341"],"isbn":["9781450363341"],"pages":"187-196","place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"ACM International Conference Proceeding Series","status":"p","subtitle":"SMSociety '18","title":"Proceedings of the 9th International Conference on Social Media and Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051473071"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-039fe36b-0f71-4fd9-baa9-3a567fe6ed68","itu-80c4ef17-6a44-49da-b5fa-c89f8c6074cf"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Comfortably Numb : Danish Teens’ Attitudes Towards Social Media Platforms","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.91-031076","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Online social media contain valuable quantitative and qualitative data, necessary to advance complex social systems studies. However, these data vaults are often behind a wall: the owners of the media sites dictate what, when, and how much data can be collected via a mandatory interface (called Application Program Interface: API). To work with such restrictions, network scientists have designed sampling methods, which do not require a full crawl of the data to obtain a representative picture of the underlying social network. However, such sampling methods are usually evaluated only on one dimension: what strategy allows for the extraction of a sample whose statistical properties are closest to the original network? In this paper we go beyond this view, by creating a benchmark that tests the performance of a method in a multifaceted way. When evaluating a network sampling algorithm, we take into account the API policies and the budget a researcher has to explore the network. By doing so, we show that some methods which are considered to perform poorly actually can perform well with tighter budgets, or with different API policies. Our results show that the decision of which sampling algorithm to use is not monodimensional. It is not enough to ask which method returns the most accurate sample, one has also to consider through which API constraints it has to go, and how much it can spend on the crawl.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Coscia, Michele","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382154"],"event":{"end":"2018-12-13","place":"Seattle, us","start":"2018-12-10","title":"2018 IEEE International Conference on Big Data (Big Data)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Network analysis","Social media","network sampling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"benchmarking api costs of network sampling strategies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83565384/network_sampling_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382154","identifier":[{"id":"85062609608","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3c8b5a94-25be-4acb-b274-db7f30399704"],"keyword":["Social media","network analysis","network sampling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F2E79B4449B0D004226304DD9952ADD2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83565384/network_sampling_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"cosciapau","last":"Coscia","locid":"90b501a9-4d44-460b-b193-4d7d524bb21b","name":"Coscia, Michele","orcid":"0000-0001-5984-5137","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/bigdata.2018.8622486","eisbn":["9781538650356"],"isbn":["9781538650349"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2018 IEEE International Conference on Big Data, BigData 2018"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062609608"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3c8b5a94-25be-4acb-b274-db7f30399704"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Benchmarking API Costs of Network Sampling Strategies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382154","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Survey-based studies are increasingly experimenting with strategies that employ digital footprints left by users on social media as entry points for recruiting participants and complementary data sources. In this perspective, the Facebook advertising platform provides unique opportunities and challenges through its marketing tools that target advertisements based on users’ demographics, behaviors, and interests. This paper presents a procedure that employed the most recent developments in Facebook marketing tools to evaluate the efficiency and effectiveness of an innovative method for recruiting niche and traditionally hard-to-reach respondents. Although the multiple innovations introduced in the method hinder a proper comparison with previous studies, the survey provides evidence concerning the efficacy of the procedure and offers scholars a set of implementations to design future comparable Facebook ad–based surveys. Challenges, opportunities, and results for effectiveness are discussed in light of a previous survey on Italian adults carried out with a panel-based CAWI method.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Iannelli, Laura","Giglietto, Fabio","Rossi, Luca","Zurovac, Elisabetta"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384121"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universita' degli Studi de Urbino Carlo Bo","University of Sassari"],"keyword":["Conspiracy theories","Facebook","Web survey","digital footprints"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"facebook digital traces for survey research assessing the efficiency and effectiveness of a facebook ad based procedure for recruiting online survey respondents in niche and difficult to reach populations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83633624/SSCR_18.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384121","identifier":[{"id":"85059463786","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c322a33d-264a-4dcc-aa33-f499dba17ccc"],"keyword":["Facebook","conspiracy theories","digital footprints","web survey"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-83E327A8624E3688577D182E69939564"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83633624/SSCR_18.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of sassari","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sassari","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"universita degli studi de urbino carlo bo","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universita' degli Studi de Urbino Carlo Bo","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human Data Interaction Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"iannellipau","last":"Iannelli","name":"Iannelli, Laura","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio","key":"gigliettopau","last":"Giglietto","name":"Giglietto, Fabio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabetta","key":"zurovacpau","last":"Zurovac","name":"Zurovac, Elisabetta","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0894439318816638","issn":["08944393","15528286"],"issn_org":["08944393"],"journal":"Social Science Computer Review","publisher":"Sage Publishing","status":"p","title":"Social Science Computer Review"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059463786"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c322a33d-264a-4dcc-aa33-f499dba17ccc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Facebook digital traces for survey research: Assessing the efficiency and effectiveness of a Facebook ad–based procedure for recruiting online survey respondents in niche and difficult-to-reach populations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384121","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"THESEUS is a space mission concept aimed at exploiting Gamma-Ray Bursts for investigating the early Universe and at providing a substantial advancement of multi-messenger and time-domain astrophysics. These goals will be achieved through a unique combination of instruments allowing GRB and X-ray transient detection over a broad field of view (more than 1sr) with 0.5–1 arcmin localization, an energy band extending from several MeV down to 0.3 keV and high sensitivity to transient sources in the soft X-ray domain, as well as on-board prompt (few minutes) follow-up with a 0.7 m class IR telescope with both imaging and spectroscopic capabilities. THESEUS will be perfectly suited for addressing the main open issues in cosmology such as, e.g., star formation rate and metallicity evolution of the inter-stellar and intra-galactic medium up to redshift 10, signatures of Pop III stars, sources and physics of re-ionization, and the faint end of the galaxy luminosity function. In addition, it will provide unprecedented capability to monitor the X-ray variable sky, thus detecting, localizing, and identifying the electromagnetic counterparts to sources of gravitational radiation, which may be routinely detected in the late ’20s/early ’30s by next generation facilities like aLIGO/ aVirgo, eLISA, KAGRA, and Einstein Telescope. THESEUS will also provide powerful synergies with the next generation of multi-wavelength observatories (e.g., LSST, ELT, SKA, CTA, ATHENA).","author_count":213,"contributors":["Amati, L.","O’Brien, P.","Götz, D.","Bozzo, E.","Tenzer, C.","Frontera, F.","Ghirlanda, G.","Labanti, C.","Osborne, J.P.","Stratta, G.","Tanvir, N.","Willingale, R.","Attina, P.","Campana, R.","Castro-Tirado, A.J.","Contini, C.","Fuschino, F.","Gomboc, A.","Hudec, R.","Orleanski, P.","Renotte, E.","Rodic, T.","Bagoly, Z.","Blain, A.","Callanan, P.","Covino, S.","Ferrara, A.","Le Floch, E.","Marisaldi, M.","Mereghetti, S.","Rosati, P.","Vacchi, A.","D’Avanzo, P.","Giommi, P.","Piranomonte, S.","Piro, L.","Reglero, V.","Rossi, A.","Santangelo, A.","Salvaterra, R.","Tagliaferri, G.","Vergani, S.","Vinciguerra, S.","Briggs, M.","Campolongo, E.","Ciolfi, R.","Connaughton, V.","Cordier, B.","Morelli, B.","Orlandini, M.","Adami, C.","Argan, A.","Atteia, J.-L.","Auricchio, N.","Balazs, L.","Baldazzi, G.","Basa, S.","Basak, R.","Bellutti, P.","Bernardini, M.G.","Bertuccio, G.","Braga, J.","Branchesi, M.","Brandt, Søren","Brocato, E.","Budtz-Jørgensen, Carl","Bulgarelli, A.","Burderi, L.","Camp, J.","Capozziello, S.","Caruana, J.","Casella, P.","Cenko, B.","Chardonnet, P.","Ciardi, B.","Colafrancesco, S.","Dainotti, M.G.","D’Elia, V.","De Martino, D.","De Pasquale, M.","Del Monte, E.","Della Valle, M.","Drago, A.","Evangelista, Y.","Feroci, M.","Finelli, F.","Fiorini, M.","Fynbo, J.","Gal-Yam, A.","Gendre, B.","Ghisellini, G.","Grado, A.","Guidorzi, C.","Hafizi, M.","Hanlon, L.","Hjorth, J.","Izzo, L.","Kiss, L.","Kumar, P.","Kuvvetli, Irfan","Lavagna, M.","Li, T.","Longo, F.","Lyutikov, M.","Maio, U.","Maiorano, E.","Malcovati, P.","Malesani, D.","Margutti, R.","Martin-Carrillo, A.","Masetti, N.","McBreen, S.","Mignani, R.","Morgante, G.","Mundell, C.","Nørgaard-Nielsen, Hans Ulrik","Nicastro, L.","Palazzi, E.","Paltani, S.","Panessa, F.","Pareschi, G.","Pe’er, A.","Penacchioni, A.V.","Pian, E.","Piedipalumbo, E.","Piran, T.","Rauw, G.","Razzano, M.","Read, A.","Rezzolla, L.","Romano, P.","Ruffini, R.","Savaglio, S.","Sguera, V.","Schady, P.","Skidmore, W.","Song, L.","Stanway, E.","Starling, R.","Topinka, M.","Troja, E.","van Putten, M.","Vanzella, E.","Vercellone, S.","Wilson-Hodge, C.","Yonetoku, D.","Zampa, G.","Zampa, N.","Zhang, B.B.","Zhang, B.B.","Zhang, S.","Zhang, S.","Antonelli, A.","Bianco, F.","Boci, S.","Boer, M.","Botticella, M.T.","Boulade, O.","Butler, C.","Campana, S.","Capitanio, F.","Celotti, A.","Chen, Y.","Colpi, M.","Comastri, A.","Cuby, J.-G.","Dadina, M.","De Luca, A.","Dong, Y.-W.","Ettori, S.","Gandhi, P.","Geza, E