{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Schwartz, Sander Andreas","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384060"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"facebook ftw a comparative content analysis of party leaders on facebook during 000000002011 000000002015 dk election","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384060","ids":["itu-bf19e359-faca-4343-ba20-679a8848afe0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F3DEC7B632C66FEB6137307482436BF9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human Data Interaction Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sander Andreas","key":"schwartzpau","last":"Schwartz","name":"Schwartz, Sander Andreas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bf19e359-faca-4343-ba20-679a8848afe0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Facebook - ftw! : A comparative content analysis of party leaders on Facebook during 2011/2015 DK election","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384060","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"After a request from the Europea n Commission, EFSA’s Panel on Animal Health and Welfaresummarised the main characteristics of 36 vector-borne disease s (VBDs) in 36 web-based storymaps.The risk of introduction in the EU through movement of livestock or pets was assessed for eac h of the36 VBDs individually, using a semiquantitative Metho d to INTegrate all relevant RISK aspects(MINTRI SK model), which was further modiﬁed to a European scale into the EFSA-VBD-RISK-m odel .Only eight of the 36 VBD-agents had an overall rate of introduction in the EU (being the combinationof the rate of entry, vector transmission and establishment) which was estimated to be above 0.001introductions per year. These were Crimean-Congo haemorrhagic fever virus, bluetongue virus, WestNile virus, Schmallenberg virus, Hepatozoon canis, Leishmania infantum, Bunyamwera virus andHighlands J. virus. For these eight dise ases, the annual extent of spread was assessed, assuming theimplementation of available, authorised prevention and control measures in the EU. Further, theprobability of overwintering was assessed, as well as the possible impact of the VBDs on public health,animal health and farm production. For the other 28 VBD-agents for which the rate of introduction wasestimated to be very low, no further asse ssments were made. Due to the uncertainty related to someparameters used for the risk assessment or the instable or unpredictability disease situation in some ofthe source regions, it is recommended to update the assessment when new information becomesavailable. Since this risk assessment was carried out for large regions in the EU for many VBD-agents,it should be considered as a ﬁrst screening. If a more detailed risk assessment for a speciﬁcVBDiswished for on a national or subnational level, the EFSA-VBD-RISK-model is freely available for thispurpose.","author_count":36,"contributors":["More, Simon J.","Bicout, Dominique","Bøtner, Anette","Butterworth, Andrew","Calistri, Paolo","Koeijer, Aline De","Depner, Klaus","Edwards, Sandra","Garin-Bastuji, Bruno","Good, Margaret","Gortazar Schmidt, Christian","Michel, Virginie","Miranda, Miguel Angel","Nielsen, Søren Saxmose","Raj, Mohan","Sihvonen, Liisa","Spoolder, Hans","Thulke, Hans-Hermann","Velarde, Antonio","Willeberg, Preben","Winckler, Christoph","Bau, Andrea","Beltran-Beck, Beatriz","Carnesecchi, Edoardo","Casier, Pascal","Czwienczek, Ewelina","Dhollander, Soﬁe","Georgiadis, Marios","Gogin, Andrey","Pasinato, Luca","Richardson, Jane","Riolo, Francesca","Rossi, Gianluca","Watts, Matthew","Lima, Eliana","Stegeman, Jan Arend"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-528254"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Ireland","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","EFSA Animal Health and Welfare Panel","EFSA Panel on Animal Health and Welfare","University College Dublin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vector borne diseases","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2903/j.efsa.2017.4793","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-528254","ids":["ku-e19f1153-3930-448b-a126-436cd777e4c8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AAD683EB95C73B5F0EA670531E7DF654"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/179671054/More_et_al_2017_EFSA_Journal_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2903/j.efsa.2017.4793","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ie","key":"university college dublin","loc":["Ireland","Euro