{"abstract":"In this article we discuss visualisation strategies for multiplex networks. Since Moreno’s early works on network analysis, visualisation has been one of the main ways to understand networks thanks to its ability to summarise a complex structure into a single representation highlighting multiple properties of the data. However, despite the large renewed interest in the analysis of multiplex networks, no study has proposed specialised visualisation approaches for this context and traditional methods are typically applied instead. In this paper we initiate a critical and structured discussion of this topic, and claim that the development of specific visualisation methods for multiplex networks will be one of the main drivers pushing current research results into daily practice.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Rossi, Luca","Magnani, Matteo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383011"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Analytics","Multiplex","Visualisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards effective visual analytics on multiplex and multilayer networks","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81821559/Towards_effective_visual_analytics_on_multiplex_and_multilayer_networks.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383011","identifier":[{"id":"84923364231","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7643dfe5-13c0-49e1-b65f-5c900b419e27"],"keyword":["analytics","multiplex","visualisation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3B52F421973456901BBAEDC28ED8EC50"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01666.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81821559/Towards_effective_visual_analytics_on_multiplex_and_multilayer_networks.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Matteo","key":"magnanipau","last":"Magnani","name":"Magnani, Matteo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.chaos.2014.12.022","issn":["09600779","18732887"],"issn_org":["09600779"],"journal":"Chaos, Solitons and Fractals","pages":"68-76","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Chaos, Solitons and Fractals","title_org":"Chaos, Solitons & Fractals","volume":"72"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84923364231"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7643dfe5-13c0-49e1-b65f-5c900b419e27"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards effective visual analytics on multiplex and multilayer networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383011","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Images and visual content in general constitute a large part of online communication. This chapter attempts a first analysis of the role played by images within a microblogging platform suggesting three categories: self-portraits, user generated content, and screenshots.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382128"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Microblogging","Screenshots","Self Portraits","User generated content","Visual communication"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chiacchierare con le immagini l uso delle fotografie nei servizi di microblogging","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.francoangeli.it/ricerca/Scheda_libro.aspx?ID=20916","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382128","ids":["itu-3ac73d97-82ac-4bdb-a53b-50139d6aaa3d"],"keyword":["Microblogging","Screenshots","Self-Portraits","User Generated Content","Visual Communication"],"lang":"Italian","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6E4D246C6F7DE36880FC622123D826F9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788820417413"],"pages":"135","publisher":"Edizioni FrancoAngeli","status":"p","subtitle":"Social effects of the Web. Forms of communication and research methods for online research.","title":"Gli effetti sociali del web. Forme della comunicazione e metodologie della ricerca online"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3ac73d97-82ac-4bdb-a53b-50139d6aaa3d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Chiacchierare con le immagini, l'uso delle fotografie nei servizi di microblogging","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382128","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The Large Observatory For x-ray Timing (LOFT) was studied within ESA M3 Cosmic Vision framework and participated in the final down-selection for a launch slot in 2022-2024. Thanks to the unprecedented combination of effective area and spectral resolution of its main instrument, LOFT will study the behaviour of matter under extreme conditions, such as the strong gravitational field in the innermost regions of accretion flows close to black holes and neutron stars, and the supra-nuclear densities in the interior of neutron stars. The science payload is based on a Large Area Detector (LAD, 10 m 2 effective area, 2-30 keV, 240 eV spectral resolution, 1 deg collimated field of view) and a WideField Monitor (WFM, 2-50 keV, 4 steradian field of view, 1 arcmin source location accuracy, 300 eV spectral resolution). The WFM is equipped with an on-board system for bright events (e.g. GRB) localization. The trigger time and position of these events are broadcast to the ground within 30 s from discovery. In this paper we present the status of the mission at the end of its Phase A study.","author_count":344,"contributors":["Feroci, M.","Herder, J. W. den","Bozzo, E.","Barret, D.","Brandt, Søren","Hernanz, M.","van der Klis, M.","Pohl, M.","Santangelo, A.","Stella, L.","Watts, A.","Wilms, J.","Zane, S.","Ahangarianabhari, M.","Albertus, C.","Alford, M.","Alpar, A.","Altamirano, D.","Alvarez, L.","Amati, L.","Amoros, C.","Andersson, N.","Antonelli, A.","Argan, A.","Artigue, R.","Artigues, B.","Atteia, J. -L.","Azzarello, P.","Bakala, P.","Baldazzi, G.","Balman, S.","Barbera, M.","van Baren, C.","Bhattacharyya, S.","Baykal, A.","Belloni, T.","Bernardini, F.","Bertuccio, G.","Bianchi, S.","Bianchini, A.","Binko, P.","Blay, P.","Bocchino, F.","Bodin, P.","Bombaci, I.","Bidaud, J. -M. Bonnet","Boutloukos, S.","Bradley, L.","Braga, J.","Brown, E.","Bucciantini, N.","Burderi, L.","Burgay, M.","Bursa, M.","Budtz-Jørgensen, Carl","Cackett, E.","Cadoux, F. R.","Cais, P.","Calia