vatory for x-ray timing","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-705568","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we address the issue of how emotional stability affects social relationships in Twitter. In particular, we focus our study on users’ communicative interactions, identified by the symbol “@.” We collected a corpus of about 200,000 Twitter posts, and we annotated it with our personality recognition system. This system exploits linguistic features, such as punctuation and emoticons, and statistical features, such as follower count and retweeted posts. We tested the system on a data set annotated with personality models produced by human subjects and against a software for the analysis of Twitter data. Social network analysis shows that, whereas secure users have more mutual connections, neurotic users post more than secure ones and have the tendency to build longer chains of interacting users. Clustering coefficient analysis reveals that, whereas secure users tend to build stronger networks, neurotic users have difficulty in belonging to a stable community; hence, they seek for new contacts in online social networks.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Celli, Fabio","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381813"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Trento"],"keyword":["Data mining","Personality Recognition","Social network analysis","Twitter"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long chains or stable communities the role of emotional stability in twitter conversations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/coin.12023","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381813","identifier":[{"id":"84922697353","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2461167a-68e6-42c6-9374-3c1a064d6aad"],"keyword":["Data Mining","Personality Recognition","Social Network Analysis","Twitter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FECB87D779B4CF8F1F9300DE7CEFD719"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/coin.12023","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://doi.wiley.com/10.1111/coin.12023","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of trento","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Trento","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture, Aesthetics, Organisations and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio","key":"cellipau","last":"Celli","name":"Celli, Fabio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/coin.12023","issn":["08247935","14678640"],"issn_org":["08247935"],"issue":"1","journal":"Computational Intelligence","pages":"184-200","paperid":"7","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Computational Intelligence","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2461167a-68e6-42c6-9374-3c1a