{"abstract":"A relevant feature of Social Network Sites is their ability to propagate units of information and create large distributed conversations. This phenomenon is particularly relevant because of the speed of information propagation, which is known to be much faster than within traditional media, and because of the very large amount of people that can potentially be exposed to information items. While many general formal models of network propagation have been developed in different research fields, in this chapter we present the result of an empirical study on a Large Social Database (LSD) aimed at measuring specific socio-technical factors enabling information spreading in Social Network Sites.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Magnani, Matteo","Montesi, Danilo","Rossi, Luca"],"cuid":["S02-080.00-767997"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"factors enabling information propagation in a social network site","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-7091-1346-2_18","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-080.00-767997","ids":["au-f0ffcbca-a490-439a-a941-ac74f9eead09","itu-a7540df1-61bf-4880-bd02-d45e03f8be60"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4993516FAACFE129EC91F5E38281642F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-7091-1346-2_18","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-7091-1346-2_18","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture, Aesthetics, Organisations and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matteo","key":"magnanipau","last":"Magnani","locid":"166a0bc9-dc53-4d62-a305-e1f1d9729619","name":"Magnani, Matteo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Danilo","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","name":"Montesi, Danilo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tansel","key":"özyerpedh","last":"Özyer","name":"Özyer, Tansel","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jon","key":"roknepedh","last":"Rokne","name":"Rokne, Jon","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gerhard","key":"wagnerpedh","last":"Wagner","name":"Wagner, Gerhard","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Arno H.P.","key":"reuserpedh","last":"Reuser","name":"Reuser, Arno H.P.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-7091-1346-2_18","eisbn":["9783709113462"],"isbn":["9783709113455"],"issn":["21905428"],"pages":"411-426","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Social Networks","status":"p","title":"The Influence of Technology on Social Network Analysis and Mining"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f0ffcbca-a490-439a-a941-ac74f9eead09","itu-a7540df1-61bf-4880-bd02-d45e03f8be60"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Factors Enabling Information Propagation in a Social Network Site","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.00-767997","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"During crisis events individuals look for information and try to share useful content or testify their own experience through social media. The research for valuable information is, relies largely on information provided by news agencies and official actors. This collective behavior leads, on a given amount of time, toward the emergence of gatewatching activities where digital media are used to reshare and to control information. This paper will investigate how this phenomenon emerge looking at the Twitter conversations produced during the first five hours after the earthquake that struck Emilia Romagna region in Italy on May 20th 2012. We have been able to detect, in the early user-led phase of the phenomenon, what kind of messages were produced and how user-produced communication results in different network structures.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Rossi, Luca","Zurovac, Elisabetta"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-385003"],"event":{"end":"2013-10-26","place":"Denver, us","start":"2013-10-23","title":"Internet Research 14.0: Resistance and Appropriation","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Crisis communication","Gatewatching","Network Structures","Social media","Twitter Analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the genesis of crisis communication in twitter from witnesses to gatewatchers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://spir.aoir.org/index.php/spir/article/view/817/pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-385003","ids":["itu-feb5200d-e1a1-4876-9343-0c7e81285856"],"keyword":["Crisis Communication","Gatewatching","Network Structures","Social Media","Twitter Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-77A2BF1A30B0EF3861144507F61F9700"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://spir.aoir.org/index.php/spir/article/view/817/pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture, Aesthetics, Organisations and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabetta","key":"zurovacpau","last":"Zurovac","name":"Zurovac, Elisabetta","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["21623317"],"journal":"Selected Papers of Internet Research","status":"p","title":"Selected Papers of Internet Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-feb5200d-e1a1-4876-9343-0c7e81285856"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Genesis of Crisis Communication in Twitter: from Witnesses to Gatewatchers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-385003","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"A precision measurement by the Alpha Magnetic Spectrometer on the International Space Station of the positron fraction in primary cosmic rays in the energy range from 0.5 to 350 GeV based on 6.8×106 positron and electron events is presented. The very accurate data show that the positron fraction is steadily increasing from 10 to ∼250 GeV, but, from 20 to 250 GeV, the slope decreases by an order of magnitude. The positron fraction spectrum shows no fine structure, and the positron to electron ratio shows no observable anisotropy. Together, these features show the existence of new physical phenomena.","author_count":348,"contributors":["Aguilar, Mario Sánchez","Alberti, G.","Alpat, B.","Alvino, A.","Ambrosi, G.","Andeen, K.","Anderhub, H.","Arruda, L.","Azzarello, P.","Bachlechner, A.","Barao, F.","Baret, B.","Barrau, A.","Barrin, L.","Bartoloni, A.","Basara, L.","Basili, A.","Batalha, L.","Bates, J.","Battiston, R.","Bazo, J.","Becker, R.","Becker, U.","Behlmann, M.","Beischer, B.","Berdugo, J.","Berges, P.","Bertucci, B.","Bigongiari, G.","Biland, A.","Bindi, V.","Bizzaglia, S.","Boella, G.","De Boer, Willem Adriaan","Bollweg, K.","Bolmont, J.","Borgia, B.","Borsini, S.","Boschini, M.J.","Boudoul, G.","Bourquin, M.","Brun, P.","Buénerd, M.","Burger, James E.","Burger, W.","Cadoux, F.","Cai, X.D.","Capell, M.","Casadei, D.","Casaus, J.","Cascioli, V.","Castellini, G.","Cernuda, I.","Cervelli, F.","Chae, M.J.","Chang, Yuanyuan","Chen, A.I.","Chen, C.R.","Chen, H.","Cheng, G.M.","Chen, H.S.","Cheng, L.","Chernoplyiokov, N.","Chikanian, A.","Choumilov, E.","Choutko, V.","Chung, Charissa","Clark, C.","Clavero, R.","Coignet, G.","Commichau, V.","Consolandi, C.","Contin, A.","Corti, C.","Costado Dios, M.T.","Coste, B.","Crespo, D.","Cui, Z.","Dai, M.","Delgado, C.","Della Torre, S.","Demirkoz, B.","Dennett, P.","Derome, L.","Di Falco, S.","Diao, X.H.","Diago, A.","Djambazov, L.","Díaz, C.","Von Doetinchem, P.","Du, W.J.","Dubois, J.M.","Duperay, R.","Duranti, 